pass@1 uses the unbiased estimator described by Mark Chen and coauthors in
"Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code", arXiv:2107.03374
(https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.03374). That paper's tasks and code are not
included. The citation is not an endorsement.

The comparison runner starts the Claude Code executable. Claude Code is a
product name, not an AIC component. Its command-line contract was checked
against Anthropic's headless documentation on 2026-11-07:
https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless
That documentation was not copied. AIC does not relicense Claude Code.

Reported cost is the `total_cost_usd` value printed by Claude Code. This
benchmark does not apply a token price table and does not invent a cost when
that field is absent.
